      "mergedAt": "2026-10-15T07:40:41Z",
      "labels": [
        "css-overflow-4",
        "Closed Accepted by Editor Discretion",
        "topic: line-clamp"
      ],
      "hint": "unknown",
      "release": "⏳ 未リリース",
      "body": "This is a follow up to https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12859. The resolution taken there had no intent to change any effect on layouts, but without clarification in the spec text, it could be inferred that the clamped lines are still taken into account not only for accessibility / interactivity reasons, but also for layout reasons, and that was not indented. It would also break compat with the legacy -webkit-line-clamp verison.",
